node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
# The whole infra/ tree, not just infra/edd-workbench/cdk.out — no app
# image needs the CDK code at all, and excluding only cdk.out wasn't
# reliable: cdk.out lives *inside* infra/edd-workbench, which is inside the
# same repo root used as the Docker build context, so a synth run reading
# its own in-progress cdk.out as part of that context (however briefly)
# self-referentially nested asset copies inside each other until
# `mkdir` hit ENAMETOOLONG. Excluding the whole parent directory removes
# the self-reference instead of relying on precisely excluding the one
# moving-target subdirectory inside it.
infra
# Real local-dev secrets, never baked into an image — discovered the hard
# way: without this, the local .env got copied straight into the server
# image, and loadEnv.ts's dotenv.config() then set DATABASE_URL from it
# (dotenv doesn't override already-set vars, but DATABASE_URL wasn't one of
# the vars the deployed task sets — only DB_HOST/PORT/USERNAME/PASSWORD
# are), which resolveConnectionString prefers over the DB_HOST/PORT
# fallback. The deployed migration task would have silently tried
# connecting to localhost:5432 instead of the real RDS endpoint every time.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example
